(
    version: 1,
    id: "m08",
    title: "Line Follower I",
    chapter: 3,
    concepts: ["On-off control", "P control"],
    world: (id: "line_track", variant: Some("a")),
    robot: Starter("rover"),
    time_limit_s: 65.0,
    grading_seeds: [1, 2, 3],
    battery_soc: (0.7, 1.0),
    brief_md: r#"
## One lap of the oval

Follow the black line around the oval, once, in **60 seconds or less**, and never go more than
**40 mm from the line**. The Rover starts on the line.

The colour sensor under the front of the Rover tells you how bright the floor is: low over the black
line, high over the white mat. One sensor cannot tell you *which side* of the line you are on, but it
can tell you whether you are on the **edge** of it: follow the edge, and steer left when the sensor sees
white and right when it sees black.

*Bang-bang* control turns by a fixed amount either way. *P control* turns by an amount that grows
with how far the reading is from the edge value.
"#,
    predict: Some((
        question: "What reflect value (0 to 100) does the colour sensor read when it is over the black line?",
        unit: "%",
        measured: "reflect_on_line",
    )),
    criteria: [FollowLine(max_dev_m: 0.04, laps: 1, within_s: 60.0)],
    stars: (
        (text: "A lap in under 30 seconds", criteria: [FollowLine(max_dev_m: 0.04, laps: 1, within_s: 30.0)]),
        (text: "Never more than 20 mm from the line", criteria: [FollowLine(max_dev_m: 0.02, laps: 1, within_s: 30.0)]),
    ),
    hints: (
        "Print axl_color_reflect for a few seconds while you drive over the line by hand (a fixed turn) and note the value over black and over white.",
        "The edge of the line reads about half way between black and white. error = reading - edge_value. Steer with left = base + k * error and right = base - k * error.",
        "If the Rover wobbles, lower k or lower base. If it loses the line in a curve, raise k. Slow down when the error is large.",
    ),
)
